{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "23", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "11", "S": "40"}}, "news": [{"title": "Odisha eyes 30,000 affordable houses under PMAY-Urban 2.0", "para": "Odisha plans to build thousands of affordable and rental homes statewide. Detailed project reports and technical support will come from consultancy firms working on this initiative. Major urban centers such as Bhubaneswar and Cuttack will receive a large portion of these housing developments, which focus on sustainable, climate-resilient designs in accordance with the PMAY-U 2.0 scheme for urban poor and middle-class households.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/odisha-eyes-30000-affordable-houses-under-pmay-urban-2-0/133437433?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-331366/133437433.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Goa: Builder told to pay \u20b919.7 lakh maintenance dues on unsold units", "para": "A developer is required to settle maintenance dues amounting to almost twenty lakh rupees for unsold units within a housing complex in Margao. The governing authority has determined that builders are responsible for maintenance costs on all unsold areas. Despite the developer contesting this ruling, their objections were dismissed, and they are obligated to pay both the outstanding balance and ongoing monthly maintenance fees.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/goa-builder-told-to-pay-19-7-lakh-maintenance-dues-on-unsold-units/133437413?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-49842/133437413.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Ageing Delhi colonies to get a chance to rebuild, grow under master plan 2047", "para": "Delhi's Master Plan 2047 outlines a strategy to rejuvenate aging government colonies and housing societies. To initiate redevelopment, a minimum plot size of 3,000 square metres is necessary for any new construction. Residents have the option to combine properties for modernization, leading to improved living conditions and amenities. Additionally, any new road development must gain approval before projects can begin.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ageing-delhi-colonies-to-get-a-chance-to-rebuild-grow-under-master-plan-2047/133419799?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-278324/133419799.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}